  "name": "xilem",
  "description": "Xilem is an experimental reactive UI framework for Rust that implements a retained-mode architecture using lightweight view objects and tree diffing. Drawing inspiration from Flutter, SwiftUI, and Elm, it separates high-level view logic from a stable widget tree managed by the Masonry toolkit. The framework leverages Vello for GPU-accelerated 2D graphics and Parley for advanced text layout, emphasizing strong typing and efficient state reconciliation.",
